From 6de2efa150b6b6756e0fcc09d2b744f443b8bcf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Huth <benjamin@laminar.network>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 05:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ceph: ignore atime flags when comparing superblocks

ceph_set_super() unconditionally sets SB_NODIRATIME and SB_NOATIME
because CephFS does not maintain atime. These flags are absent from
fc->sb_flags: the VFS handles noatime and nodiratime as per-mount flags.
However, ceph_compare_super() masks only SB_BORN before comparing the
existing superblock's flags with those in the new mount request.

As a result, otherwise identical mounts fail the flags comparison and
allocate separate superblocks and clients instead of sharing them. This
creates extra MDS sessions and prevents inode cache sharing, which is
particularly noticeable with many Kubernetes pods mounting the same
CephFS path.

Mask SB_NODIRATIME and SB_NOATIME along with SB_BORN when comparing the
superblock flags. Keep the atime flags set on the superblock so that
atime updates remain disabled, and preserve the comparison of the other
superblock flags.

Fixes: f7a2d0688a3b ("ceph: disable updating the atime since cephfs won't maintain it")
Closes: https://tracker.ceph.com/issues/78440
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
---
Added SB_ACTIVE in order to keep up with the new changes being made upstream:
https://github.com/ceph/ceph-client/commit/b9d944f1c8c2044d08609fdc238d27df29483e9d



 fs/ceph/super.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/ceph/super.c b/fs/ceph/super.c
index 72935f665f11..13a8f246f1a0 100644
--- a/fs/ceph/super.c
+++ b/fs/ceph/super.c
@@ -1265,7 +1265,8 @@ static int ceph_compare_super(struct super_block *sb, struct fs_context *fc)
 		doutc(cl, "fsid doesn't match\n");
 		return 0;
 	}
-	if (fc->sb_flags != (sb->s_flags & ~SB_BORN)) {
+	if (fc->sb_flags != (sb->s_flags &
+			     ~(SB_BORN | SB_NODIRATIME | SB_NOATIME | SB_ACTIVE))) {
 		doutc(cl, "flags differ\n");
 		return 0;
 	}

base-commit: dc173b37415e8f738fc4de477490056b479ddc9f
